<%- include("partials/header") %>

<section class="hero" style="padding-block:clamp(2.5rem,6vw,4rem)">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="reveal" style="max-width:46rem">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="display-lg" style="margin-block:1rem 1.25rem">
        A journal that lives entirely on <span class="accent" style="color:var(--accent);font-style:italic">your machine</span>.
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Inkora is a local-first personal blog: an Express server, a handful of EJS
        templates, and one carefully set stylesheet. No database, no accounts, no
        tracking pixels.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="shell about-grid">
    <div class="prose reveal" data-delay="1">
      <h2 class="display-sm" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Why it is built this way</h2>
      <p>
        Most writing tools ask you to manage something other than your writing.
        Inkora deliberately asks for nothing. You start the server, the journal is
        there, you close the terminal, and it is gone &mdash; which is an honest
        way to build a demo and a useful constraint for a portfolio piece.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>The whole application can be read in one sitting.</strong> That is
        treated as a feature rather than a limitation. Every route lives in a
        single <code>index.js</code>, every pixel is defined by CSS custom
        properties at the top of <code>styles.css</code>, and the progressive
        behaviour &mdash; theme preference, mobile navigation, reading progress
        &mdash; is a few dozen lines of dependency-free JavaScript.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-sm" style="margin-block:2.25rem 1rem">The editorial system</h2>
      <p>
        Type does the heavy lifting. <strong>Fraunces</strong> sets the display
        headlines with its optical sizing and wonk axis turned up, so large sizes
        get their high-contrast details. <strong>Newsreader</strong> carries the
        article body at a 68-character measure with 1.78 line height, which is
        where long-form prose stops being a wall. <strong>Inter</strong> handles
        everything that is interface: navigation, metadata, buttons and form
        labels.
      </p>
      <p>
        The palette is warm ink on paper rather than pure black on pure white,
        with a single oxblood accent used sparingly for links, kickers and the
        drop cap. A faint paper grain sits over the whole page, and the dark
        theme is a genuine re-token of the same system rather than an inverted
        copy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-sm" style="margin-block:2.25rem 1rem">What you can do here</h2>
      <p>
        Publish an entry with a title, comma-separated topics and a body. Read it
        on its own page with a drop cap, a reading-progress rule and related
        entries underneath. Revise it, and the entry is stamped with the revision
        date. Search across titles, bodies and topics, or filter the feed by a
        single topic from the rail under the masthead.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top:1.5rem">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/">
          Read the journal
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="panel reveal" data-delay="2">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem">By the numbers</p>

      <div class="stat-row" style="margin-top:0">
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat__value tnum"><%= stats.posts %></div>
          <div class="stat__label">Entries</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat__value tnum"><%= stats.tags %></div>
          <div class="stat__label">Topics</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat__value tnum"><%= stats.words.toLocaleString("en-US") %></div>
          <div class="stat__label">Words</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <hr class="rule" style="margin-block:1.75rem" />

      <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:1rem">Colophon</p>
      <dl class="spec-list">
        <div><dt>Runtime</dt><dd>Node.js (ES modules)</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Framework</dt><dd>Express 5</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Templates</dt><dd>EJS 5</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Body parsing</dt><dd>body-parser</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Styling</dt><dd>Hand-written CSS, custom properties</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Display type</dt><dd>Fraunces</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Text type</dt><dd>Newsreader</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Interface type</dt><dd>Inter</dd></div>
        <div><dt>JavaScript</dt><dd>Vanilla, no dependencies</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Storage</dt><dd>In-memory array</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Build step</dt><dd>None</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include("partials/footer") %>
